{
  "name": "Check in event attendees by webhook and post live counts to Slack",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Check in event attendees by webhook and post live counts to Slack\n\n**Who's it for**\nOrganisers of meetups, workshops and small conferences who sell tickets anywhere and check people in with a phone. The door team gets an instant answer and the rest of the team sees the room fill up in Slack.\n\n**How it works**\n1. Your scanner app posts each scanned code to a webhook. Codes are compared without case, spaces or dashes, so \"tix-0007\" matches \"TIX 0007\".\n2. The code is looked up in the Attendees tab. Unknown codes get a 404, codes already used get a 409 with the time of the first scan, and valid ones a 200 with the name and ticket type.\n3. A valid check-in is stamped in the checked_in_at column.\n4. Every 25th check-in, and the moment everyone has arrived, Slack gets the count, the share of the list and the count per ticket type.\n\n**How to set up**\n1. Run it once as imported from `Run manually`. A sample scan becomes check-in 25 and the run stops at `STOP: preview - nothing posted` and `STOP: not live - sheet untouched`.\n2. Connect Google Sheets and set `ATTENDEES_SHEET_ID`. The tab needs ticket_code, name, ticket_type and checked_in_at columns.\n3. Point your scanner app at the production webhook URL with a JSON body like {\"code\": \"TIX-0007\", \"gate\": \"Main\"}. Connect Slack and set `SLACK_CHANNEL_ID`.\n4. Set `TEST_EMAIL` to any address to post milestones with a [TEST] prefix. Set `TEST_RUN = false` on the day so check-ins are written to the sheet.\n\n**Requirements**\n- A Google Sheet with the attendee list\n- A scanner app that can POST JSON\n- A Slack workspace\n\n**How to customize**\n- `MILESTONE_EVERY` sets how often Slack hears about the count.\n- `CODE_PREFIX` is added to bare numbers, so a scan of \"7\" can match \"TIX0007\".\n- `ALLOW_REENTRY` lets the same ticket in again and answers 200 with a warning.",
        "height": 1056,
        "width": 520,
        "color": 4
      },
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -600,
        0
      ],
      "id": "37fd1fe0-5717-4c4e-9a00-37fd1fe013e7",
      "name": "Template overview"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 1. Receive the scan\n\nThe scanner posts to `Ticket scan webhook`, which waits for a respond node so the door gets its answer in the same request. A manual run feeds `Load sample scan` through the same path.",
        "height": 848,
        "width": 1296,
        "color": 7
      },
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        0,
        0
      ],
      "id": "85937995-5717-4c4e-9a00-859379951000",
      "name": "Section 1 note"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 2. Read the attendee list\n\nThe list is read on every scan so late registrations and manual fixes in the sheet count straight away. `Load sample attendee list` has 24 people already in, so the sample scan lands on a milestone.",
        "height": 848,
        "width": 640,
        "color": 7
      },
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        1344,
        0
      ],
      "id": "84937802-5717-4c4e-9a00-849378021001",
      "name": "Section 2 note"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 3. Validate and answer the door\n\nA ticket is used if the sheet says so or static data saw it, which catches two scans a second apart. Each outcome gets its own HTTP status so the scanner app can show red or green.",
        "height": 848,
        "width": 640,
        "color": 7
      },
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        2032,
        0
      ],
      "id": "8393766f-5717-4c4e-9a00-8393766f1002",
      "name": "Section 3 note"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 4. Stamp the sheet and post milestones\n\nOnly a live first entry writes checked_in_at. `Write the milestone post` branches off the answer, so a slow Slack call never holds up the queue at the door.",
        "height": 848,
        "width": 1072,
        "color": 7
      },
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        2720,
        0
      ],
      "id": "829374dc-5717-4c4e-9a00-829374dc1003",
      "name": "Section 4 note"
    },
    {
      "id": "bf494fa0-c3b2-4da0-a360-53606b63bf49",
      "name": "config",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "parameters": {
        "jsCode": "// CHECK IN EVENT ATTENDEES BY WEBHOOK AND POST LIVE COUNTS TO SLACK - CONFIG\n// Edit values only in this node. Nothing else in this workflow needs changing.\n// ATTENDEES_SHEET_ID blank -> a SAMPLE attendee list with 24 people already in.\n// The scanner always gets an answer; only a live run writes to the sheet.\n\n// Google Sheets id with an Attendees tab; blank uses the sample list\nconst ATTENDEES_SHEET_ID = '';\n// shown in the Slack posts\nconst EVENT_NAME = 'Ops Meetup, November';\n// post the count to Slack every this many check-ins\nconst MILESTONE_EVERY = 25;\n// prefix added to bare numeric codes; blank to turn off\nconst CODE_PREFIX = 'TIX';\n// digits after the prefix, for padding bare numbers\nconst CODE_DIGITS = 4;\n// true -> a second scan of the same ticket is let in with a warning\nconst ALLOW_REENTRY = false;\n// channel for milestone posts; blank skips Slack\nconst SLACK_CHANNEL_ID = '';\n// ships true. Nothing reaches a real recipient or system.\nconst TEST_RUN = true;\n// blank -> preview only. Set -> sends go here instead. Never causes a send on its own.\nconst TEST_EMAIL = '';\n\nconst MODE = TEST_RUN !== true ? 'live' : (TEST_EMAIL.trim() !== '' ? 'test' : 'preview');\n\nreturn [{\n  json: {\n    attendees_sheet_id: ATTENDEES_SHEET_ID,\n    event_name: EVENT_NAME,\n    milestone_every: MILESTONE_EVERY,\n    code_prefix: CODE_PREFIX,\n    code_digits: CODE_DIGITS,\n    allow_reentry: ALLOW_REENTRY,\n    slack_channel_id: SLACK_CHANNEL_ID,\n    test_run: TEST_RUN,\n    test_email: TEST_EMAIL,\n    sheet_enabled: ATTENDEES_SHEET_ID.trim() !== '',\n    slack_enabled: SLACK_CHANNEL_ID.trim() !== '',\n    mode: MODE,\n    live: MODE === 'live',\n    sends_enabled: MODE !== 'preview',\n    run_started_at: new Date().toISOString()\n  }\n}];\n"
      },
      "position": [
        272,
        176
      ]
    },
